<!--Post: 426--><!--Time: 1089602967-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST426"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ryan_olesin<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ryan_olesin<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, July 11, 2004 - 8:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This is on AMW&#39;s website and I don&#39;t recall hearing of this anywhere else. <BR> <BR><i>A postal clerk actually talked to BTK when he came in at 4 a.m. on June 16, 1979, to mail a letter to KAKE-TV.  <BR>She described him as a white male -- about 30 years old and about five feet nine inches tall. He was wearing a blue jean jacket, jeans and gloves. He was clean shaven, with hair cropped short above the ears. He had a gap between his front teeth.</i> <BR> <BR>Here&#39;s the link to read more: <BR><a href="http://www.amw.com/fugitives/bolo.cfm?id=26563" target=_top>http://www.amw.com/fugitives/bolo.cfm?id=26563</a> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 426-->
<!--Post: 429--><!--Time: 1089607784-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST429"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, July 11, 2004 - 9:49 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks Ryan; that&#39;s one facet I&#39;ve been negligent with. Certainly a very important witness. I have to think there&#39;s more info published about her encounter, but I haven&#39;t gotten around yet to finding it. Yet.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 429-->
<!--Post: 1221--><!--Time: 1097787022-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1221"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nostone<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nostone<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, October 14, 2004 - 1:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Any news on this Tom?  I&#39;m interested to hear more about this.  Could be a very valuable clue.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1221-->
<!--Post: 1425--><!--Time: 1100963910-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1425"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, November 20, 2004 - 7:18 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have always been facinated by this encounter. Was she behind the counter? Was she getting mail from an outside drop box? Surely at that early hour, BTK expected not to meet someone face to face. BTK does seem to be an early riser. <BR> <BR>Gap in teeth: a makeup pencil will create the appearance of a gap or missing tooth, if the need arises. A legitimate gap often indicates British/English ancestry. Just a thought.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1425-->
<!--Post: 1613--><!--Time: 1102323538-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1613"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 06, 2004 - 12:58 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The postal clerk may have surprised BTK. He went to the post office to mail the letter and I believe it was an indoors lobby-type drop off when all of a sudden she came out from a closed door. He even spoke to her asking her to send the letter to KAKE-TV. She seemed very discriptive of him by remembering his clothing, gapped teeth and haircut. Being so careful about her observations she said he was about 30. That would put him born in about 1949 not 1939 like in the BTK self-profile.  <BR>She&#39;s got to be one of the most important witnesses.  <BR>Was it BTK who didn&#39;t think anyone else would be at the post office, or not taking any chances did BTK ask someone to drop it off for him? If it was someone other than BTK it was either a friend or accomplice who remained quite or someone BTK asked to drop it off. If it wasn&#39;t BTK then it may have silenced that person. Did anyone matching that discription, a man of about 30 show up dead or murdered in the Wichita area during the last weeks of June 1979? Since this man was wearing gloves in June we would have to assume that this was in fact BTK protecting his fingerprints from being transfered. Unless it was a man who was a knowing accomplice to BTK in at least one of the crimes.  <BR>At 4 am this also implies that this man was probably a resident of the Wichita area.  <BR>His hair was cropped short above the ears seems to imply that his hair was a little shorter than what many men were wearing in 1979. Sounds like the kind of haircut that used to be called &#39;whitewalls.&#39; This would have been a guy who regulary went to a barber, maybe every three weeks and the same barber every time. Did the police question any of the Wichita barbers who cut hair the old fashioned way in the era of stylists becoming the norm? A customer who was a little bit strange and may have had many converstaions with his barber about the BTK murders or a more than average interest in the unsolved murders. A guy can open up on some topics more freely with his barber or bartender than with his friends or family.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1613-->
<!--Post: 1644--><!--Time: 1102511555-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1644"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ace<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ace<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 08, 2004 - 5:12 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m not so sure the postal clerk spoke or saw the BTK. The Bright victim stated the BTK had dark brown eyes and was dark complected. The postal clerk describes a W/M with a gap in his teeth. <BR>Plus WPD recently obtained a search warrent on Salvez hispanic decent. Otero family was of hispanic decent and the baby picture is off a dark complected baby. No my friends I think our boy may be of hispanic decent.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1644-->
<!--Post: 1666--><!--Time: 1102550533-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1666"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 08, 2004 - 4:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ken Stephens, a former Eagle reporter looked at his old notes from the time of 1979 and said &#34;A female postal clerk opened the door and he was standing there. He said &#39;Put this in the KAKE box&#39; and handed her the envelope.&#34; Police discounted her discription saying there was little reason for her to pay attention to the man. It seems she gave a very detailed description of the man however in that he was a white male, 5&#39;10&#34;, clean shaven with hair cropped short above the ears, waering a blue jean jacet, jeans and gloves and gapped front teeth. That sounds like she was paying attention to the man and being alone with someone you don&#39;t know at 4 in the morning I would think that would give her every reason to be paying attention. <BR> All the witness accounts vary.  <BR>In 1974 two nieghbors of the Oero&#39;s believed they saw a man leaving the house and hanging around the house. One said he was a male, dark complected and wearing a hat. The other said he was a white male, 6 feet tall with dark shaggy hair. <BR>In 1974 BTK survivor Kevin Bright said he was a  male with a slight dark compexion 5&#39;10&#34;, 180 pounds with a dark mustache and a black stockingcap pulled down almost covering the eyes wearing camoflage. <BR>In 1977 the witness to the man at the phonebooth after the Fox murder said he was a white male, 6 feet tall with blonde hair. <BR>In 1977 The Vian children because of their young ages of 4, 6 and 8 years old could not be called reliable witnesses described him as 30-40, dark haired and pot-bellied. Of course little kids might think a man of 19 is 40 in their eyes so discount the age but they did remember dark hair and what is intereting here is they said pot-bellied. Someone a little overweight around the middle is something they may remember in my opinion. <BR>Most investigators belive Bright to be the best witness however because of his wounds and stress at the time they don&#39;t consider him 100% reliable. Common denominators with Brights description is the same hieght as the postal worker&#39;s and at 5&#39;10&#34; and 180 pounds may have had a pot belly as the Vian children remembered and dark hair as they described. The dark complexion and hat also matches up with one of the Otera neighbors recolection. <BR>He is commanding and to the point when confronting people or victims. His phraseology is interesting. He told the Bright victims according to Kevin to &#34;Hold it right there.&#34;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1666-->
<!--Post: 1669--><!--Time: 1102566041-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1669"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 08, 2004 - 8:20 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I do not think the descriptions that Johno describes above are all that different.  One Otero neighbor said hat, one said dark shaggy hair.  It was January and I remember that year was a COLD winter &#40;I lived then in Stillwater, OK, about 110 miles due south of Wichita&#41; so maybe what looks like a wooly dark cap to one looks like shaggy dark hair to another.  Many white&#40;the PC term now is caucasian&#41;people are &#39;dark complected&#34;.  The height difference of 2&#34; is well within the typical error range of eyewitnesses and as to the blond hair, wigs were availible then. As to the pot-belly vs. trim, how many people&#39;s weight fluctuates? <BR>I agree with Johno about the postal worker&#39;s description.  Not trying to brag, but both my education and my hobby have taught me more about visual memory than most people know and I&#39;d bet the post office lady&#39;s description is the best of the lot.  By far.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1669-->
<!--Post: 2428--><!--Time: 1103657287-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2428"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ashdana<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ashdana<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 21, 2004 - 11:28 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->An observation: After being seen by a witness &#40;Kevin Bright&#41;, the next witness reports his hair as blond. Back in the mid 70&#39;s &#40;when I was a teenager&#41;, Sun In hair lightener was a cheap, easily available and easily used product. Even without sun, you could saturate your hair and use a hair dryer, blow dryer, or heat lamp to activate it. Then you fibbed to anyone who asked you about it that you were out in the sun and it happened naturally. And not just girls used this; plenty of the guys I knew in high school were using it because the Beach-Boys-surfer-bum look was so desirable. I think BTK did something like this. Wigs are just so obvious--even the best ones, and most available styles are created for women and look absurd on men.  <BR> <BR>It&#39;s worth noting that even though his hair color is reported as lighter in 1977, there is never a direct contradiction to the dark complexion. And many people have dark complexions without any hispanic background--people of Italian, Greek, Middle Eastern descent, for example.  <BR> <BR>I also agree with Johno about the Vian kids&#39; guess at BTK&#39;s age. Kids are absolutely terrible at judging this. Anyone older than 20 is ancient to them.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2428-->
<!--Post: 2996--><!--Time: 1104361075-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2996"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 2:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->There are already discussions about the Vian children, etc. I&#39;d like to keep this thread about the postal worker who saw BTK. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2996-->
